#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Demos/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:215
msgid ""
"The CUDA path maintains high throughput across resolutions because the zero-"
"copy IPC transfer only carries a handle, not the pixel data. The CPU path "
"must copy frames from GPU to host and serialise them through the middleware, "
"so throughput drops as image size grows. At 4K (31.6 MB per frame) the CUDA "
"backend is roughly 6x faster than the raw CPU path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Tutorials/Demos/GPU-Buffer-Transport.rst:223
msgid "What to look at in the source"
msgstr ""

